[2026-03-28 19:06:01] Review findings recorded for TFT DMA/display path.
Investigation: Reviewed TM4C129E_Project/xTask/xSource/xTask9_TFT.c, ST7735 DMA write path, semaphore ownership, button-triggered period updates, and related queue/task code.
Findings:
1. Probable remaining concurrency defect is DMA bandwidth/ordering overlap: xTask9 starts channel 30 memory-to-memory clear before launching the ST7735 panel DMA, and both channel 30 and channel 13 are configured high priority. Channel 30 clear uses 1024-beat arbitration, making it the most likely source of visible display instability under tighter redraw cadence.
2. ST7735 transaction ownership is not atomic across SetAddrWindow plus DMA start. The task only waits for semaphore completion before swap, while ST7735__vSetAddrWindow itself performs many separately locked command/data writes before ST7735__enWriteBuffer16bDMA acquires the semaphore for the DMA phase. This is a structural ordering risk, though current call sites suggest it is not the primary cause of the present symptom.
3. Several DMA task/ISR shared state variables are plain static globals rather than volatile or otherwise protected, in both xTask9_TFT.c and ST7735_Write.c. This is a concurrency correctness risk and can become optimization/timing sensitive.
Validation: No code edits made. Findings prepared for user response with recommended fix strategy.
